// larger than the configured reassembly cap, when a single chunk would
// exceed the single-fragment limit, or when the message splits into
// more fragments than the per-channel window width (it can then never
// fit the in-flight quota); ErrChecksum for a channel number outside
// the session; and ErrChannelClosed when the channel's write side has
// been closed. A rejected payload is neither queued nor journaled and
// consumes no message or frame sequence, so it takes no quota.
//
// A merely quota-tight channel is no error: the call suspends without
// consuming a sequence and completes in arrival order as soon as the
// channel's in-flight count leaves room for the whole message. While
// suspended it stays on the channel's wait queue, so writes complete
// strictly in call-arrival order and the in-flight count never crosses
// the channel's current quota.
